From: arshiyaazim <arshiya.azim.1980@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:19:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(vessel): require an exact duty day and a compatible
 Mother Vessel

Release-readiness hardening of the logical order identity:

- The day must match exactly. The earlier +/-1 day tolerance could merge a
  genuine next-day order; fragments across Dhaka midnight now fail closed to
  Review instead of merging.
- Mother Vessel becomes a discriminator: same leading name word AND at most
  three edits across the normalized name. Two spellings of one vessel
  (Union Udyssy / Union odyssey) still merge; a different fleet
  (Poavosa Wisdom / Poavosa Brave, Union odyssey / Union brave) never does.
- Drafts also record parsed.orderIdentity for audit, and the logical id now
  buckets the mother family.
- Tests: mother, start date, shift, same-day fragment window, cancellation then
  a new duty, spelling normalization, arrival-order independence, and the real
  November 3 fragments.
